  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>18</mn></msub></math> be eighteen observations such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munderover><mo>&#8721;</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>18</mn></munderover><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>36</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munderover><mo>&#8721;</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>18</mn></munderover><msup><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>90</mn></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#946;</mi></math> are distinct real numbers. If the standard deviation of these observations is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>, then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is _______."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munderover><mo>&#8721;</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>18</mn></munderover><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>36</mn><mo>,</mo><munderover><mo>&#8721;</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>18</mn></munderover><msup><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>90</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><munderover><mo>&#8721;</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>18</mn></munderover><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>18</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><munderover><mo>&#8721;</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>18</mn></munderover><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#946;</mi><munderover><mo>&#8721;</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>18</mn></munderover><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>18</mn><msup><mi>&#946;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>90</mn></math></p><p>Hence <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8721;</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>90</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>18</mn><msup><mi>&#946;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>36</mn><mi>&#946;</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mo>&#8721;</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mn>18</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mo>&#8721;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mn>18</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>90</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>18</mn><msup><mi>&#946;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>36</mn><mi>&#946;</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>18</mn><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>18</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>&#946;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math></p><p>As <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#946;</mi></math> are distinct <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>|</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>|</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p>"
  }
